 "case": "N04-ACTIVATION-NEG",
 "says": "Alice keeps a personal memory source, notes, registered under a managed home, and selects it in her personal memory position; she has selected no Instructions. She opens a link to her host session and composes the session's start from a personal request that declares session.routing.activate and pins nothing. The owner returns the preparation, which names the memory position at the head she left it and fixes the frontier of notes it observed, and records the session as selected only: the routing it returns has no projection and no memory usage contract, leaves the always surface unchanged and preserves native instruction files. No activation is ever requested. Observing that preparation then writes nothing and returns nothing. The selected-only session must not receive the usage contract or any projection, no routing may add to the always surface or write a native global file, and no observation may claim the session inactive or plain.",
